{"processInformation": {"dataSetInformation": {"UUID": "db3d0bcc-d7c2-4f06-b5b3-58aaee20f105", "name": {"baseName": [{"value": "Portland Composite Cement CEM II/A-M (T-L) 42,5 R", "lang": "en"}, {"value": "Portland Composite Zement CEM II/A-M (T-L) 42,5 R", "lang": "de"}], "functionalUnitFlowProperties": [{"lang": "en"}]}, "classificationInformation": {"classification": [{"class": [{"value": "Mineralische Baustoffe", "level": 0, "classId": "1"}, {"value": "Bindemittel", "level": 1, "classId": "1.1"}, {"value": "Zement", "level": 2, "classId": "1.1.01"}], "name": "OEKOBAU.DAT"}, {"class": [{"value": "01 Basic materials and precursors", "level": 0}, {"value": "Cement, building limes and other hydraulic binders", "level": 1}, {"value": "Cement", "level": 2}], "name": "IBUCategories"}]}, "generalComment": [{"value": "Cement is a hydraulic binder. It consists of\nfinelyground, non-metallic inorganic compounds.\nCement is produced by grinding cement clinker and\nother main or minor constituents. When water is added\nto cement, a cement paste is formed, which sets and\nhardensthrough the hydration reactions. After hardening, it retains its strength and stability even under water. The declared product is a cement conforming with the composition of Portland Composite Cement CEM II/A-M (T-L) 42.5 R manufactured by Kunda Nordic Tsement AS in the plant Kunda in 2021. The calculation is based on plant-specific data.", "lang": "en"}]}, "quantitativeReference": {"referenceToReferenceFlow": [0]}, "time": {"referenceYear": 2022, "dataSetValidUntil": 2027, "other": {"anies": [{"name": "publicationDateOfEPD", "value": 1656288000000}]}}, "geography": {"locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction": {"location": "EE"}}, "technology": {"technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses": [{"value": "Cement is a hydraulic binder. It consists of finelyground, non-metallic inorganic compounds. Cement is produced by grinding cement clinker and other main or minor constituents. When water is added to cement, a cement paste is formed, which sets and hardensthrough the hydration reactions. After hardening, it retains its strength and stability even under water. The declared product is a cement conforming with the composition of Portland Composite Cement CEM II/A-M (T-L) 42.5 R manufactured by Kunda Nordic Tsement AS in the plant Kunda in 2021. The calculation is based on plant-specific data. \nTechnical data: \nThe declared cement corresponds to the 42.5 standard compressive strength class with high early strength development (R) in accordance with EN 197-1. \nDeclared unit: \nThe declared unit is 1 t of CEM II/A-M (T-L) 42,5 R.", "lang": "en"}, {"value": "Zement ist ein hydraulisches Bindemittel. Er besteht aus\nfein gemahlenen, nicht-metallischen anorganischen Verbindungen.\nZement wird durch Mahlen von Zementklinker und\nanderen Haupt- oder Nebenbestandteilen. Durch Zugabe von Wasser\nZement zugesetzt wird, entsteht ein Zementleim, der durch\ndurch die Hydratationsreaktionen aushärtet. Nach dem Aushärten behält er seine Festigkeit und Stabilität auch unter Wasser. Bei dem angemeldeten Produkt handelt es sich um einen Zement, der der Zusammensetzung von Portlandkompositzement CEM II/A-M (T-L) 42,5 R entspricht und von Kunda Nordic Tsement AS im Werk Kunda im Jahr 2021 hergestellt wird. Die Berechnung basiert auf werksspezifischen Daten. \n", "lang": "de"}], "technologicalApplicability": [{"value": "The application of cement has a large variety. It is\nmainly used as a binder for concrete and mortar. The\napplication in concrete is regulated in EN 206.\nAccording to this standard, general suitability is\nestablished for cement conforming to EN 197-1.", "lang": "en"}, {"value": "Der Einsatz von Zement ist sehr vielfältig. Er wird\nhauptsächlich als Bindemittel für Beton und Mörtel verwendet. Die\nAnwendung in Beton ist in der EN 206 geregelt.\nNach dieser Norm ist die allgemeine Eignung\nfür Zement, der der EN 197-1 entspricht, festgelegt.", "lang": "de"}]}}, "modellingAndValidation": {"LCIMethodAndAllocation": {"typeOfDataSet": "EPD", "referenceToLCAMethodDetails": [{"shortDescription": [{"value": "Cement.pdf", "lang": "en"}], "type": "source data set", "refObjectId": "ded24cd2-2560-4646-a3e0-ed913299a328"}], "other": {"anies": [{"name": "subType", "value": "specific dataset"}]}}, "dataSourcesTreatmentAndRepresentativeness": {"referenceToDataSource": [{"shortDescription": [{"value": "ecoinvent database (all versions)", "lang": "en"}], "type": "source data set", "refObjectId": "b497a91f-e14b-4b69-8f28-f50eb1576766"}, {"shortDescription": [{"value": "ecoinvent 3.6 database", "lang": "en"}], "type": "source data set", "refObjectId": "766b9973-5ee8-48a2-8098-72c8e20b369f"}], "useAdviceForDataSet": [{"value": "Scope: \nThis Environmental Product Declaration (EPD) covers the product life cycle stages A1-A3. It is valid for Portland Cement CEM II/A-M (T-L) 42,5 R, manufactured by Kunda Nordic Tsement AS in the plant Kunda, Estonia in 2021. This analysis relies on transparent, plausible and documented basis data. All the model assumptions, which influence the results, are declared. The life cycle assessment is representative for the products introduced in the declaration for the given system boundaries. \nSystem boundary: \nType of EPD: cradle-to-gate (A1-A3)\n\nFor the modelling of cement, both specific production data from HeidelbergCement and background data (especially for upstream processes) have been used. For life cycle modelling of the considered product, the verified Global Cement and Concrete Association GCCA Core model report and GCCA Project Database for EPDs of concrete and cement is used. The tool was developed by Quantis and is owned by the Global Cement and Concrete Association. The life cycle assessment in the tool has been implemented in compliance with EN 15804, the General Programme Instructions (GPI 3.01) for the International EPD® System, the product category rules c-PCR-003 Concrete and c-PCR-001 Cement. For the present study, version 3.1 of the GCCA Concrete EPD tool was used, largely being based on the database ecoinvent v3.5\n\nA significant factor regarding primary data collection is the emission measurement directly at the plant. In line with the official regulations, regular data collections are established at HeidelbergCement group. The emission data of the clinker burning process are included in this LCA study. Preferably directly measured kiln emission values in the specific plant are considered. Noise, landscape impact, vibration etc. are not within the scope of this study. In case specific kiln emission data are not available, default values are automatically used by the GCCA tool. The selected system boundaries comprise the production of cement including raw material extraction up to the finished product at the factory gate.\n\nThe product stage contains:\n\nModule A1: Extraction and processing of raw materials.\n\nModule A2: Transport of raw materials to the factory gate and internal transport.\n\nModule A3: Cement production.\n\nThe construction stage, the use stage and the disposal stage are not included in the life cycle assessment of cement.", "lang": "en"}], "other": {"anies": [{"name": "referenceToOriginalEPD", "value": {"shortDescription": {"value": "Portland Composite Cement CEM II/A-M (T-L) 42,5 R.pdf", "defaultValue": "Portland Composite Cement CEM II/A-M (T-L) 42,5 R.pdf", "lstrings": [{"lang": "en", "value": "Portland Composite Cement CEM II/A-M (T-L) 42,5 R.pdf"}]}, "type": "source data set", "uuid": {"uuid": "16ad21e6-3de4-4b11-acbe-0b79fcec763c"}, "refObjectId": "16ad21e6-3de4-4b11-acbe-0b79fcec763c", "resourceURLs": ["https://oekobaudat.de/OEKOBAU.DAT/resource/sources/16ad21e6-3de4-4b11-acbe-0b79fcec763c/Portland_Composite_Cement_CEM_IIA-M_T-L_42_5_R_15709.pdf?version=00.01.000"]}}]}}, "validation": {"review": [{"referenceToNameOfReviewerAndInstitution": [{"shortDescription": [{"value": "Institut Bauen und Umwelt e. V.", "lang": "en"}], "type": "c